      "writtenOn": "2023-04-17T06:38:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Passthrough (APF filtering) offload should start when probing starts on the interface; note this may be later than here, because if serviceInfo.Network is null, it will start whenever a new interface comes up.\n\nI think you should probably implement the \"probing started\" callback as per your TODO, and use an interface provided in the callback, instead of starting the offload here.\n\nResponse offload should only start when advertising starts (so after probing). Another reason why a flag is probably necessary when registering offload engines. That one should probably be in onRegisterServiceSucceeded.\n\nYou\u0027ll probably need a onServiceUnregistered with an interface identifier in AdvertiserCallback to stop offload with code mirroring the start (probably cleaner/less error-prone).\n\nAnother problem with starting the offload here is that the method to determine the interface index is different from the one that will actually be used by the advertiser (which uses what SocketProvider provides), so there could be mismatches.",
      "revId": "37d939f7531a6f06463c398cda7df7cf6ce1d237",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
